# arbiter npm config.
#
# The global `legacy-peer-deps=true` flag was removed (#1557): it disabled npm's
# ERESOLVE peer-dependency checking for the ENTIRE tree just to mask a single dev
# clash — madge@8 declares `peerDependencies.typescript: ^5.4.4` while arbiter pins
# typescript ^6. That global escape hatch silently hides any FUTURE peer conflict
# (a real one we would want to see), so it is replaced by a scoped fix in
# package.json `overrides`: `madge.typescript: "$typescript"` pins madge's peer to
# arbiter's own typescript spec, leaving strict peer resolution on everywhere else.
